# Veyrnox — environment variable template (NAMES ONLY, no real values).
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in.
#
# Veyrnox's WALLET core is on-device: no server holds keys, seeds, or balances
# (see CLAUDE.md I1–I5). The ONE optional backend touchpoint is an anonymous
# referral counter (Supabase) — its URL + anon key are CLIENT-EXPOSED public
# values (not secrets), and the table stores only { code, count } (no identity,
# addresses, or holdings). Leave the Supabase vars blank to disable referrals
# entirely (the client no-ops — see src/api/referralApi.js).
#
# The only genuinely sensitive values here are the *testnet* signing inputs at
# the bottom, used solely by the Node verification scripts in scripts/.

# --- App build / runtime flags (Vite, client-exposed; not secret) ---
# Demo tour with fake seeded balances. Also triggers on ?demo=1 or a persisted
# veyrnox-demo=1 in localStorage. Leave unset for a real wallet.
VITE_DEMO_MODE=

# Release build hardening toggle (1 in release builds).
VITE_RELEASE=

# Banner label shown in non-prod builds, e.g. SIT or UAT.
VITE_ENV_LABEL=

# Environment name consumed by build scripts, e.g. production | sit | uat.
VITE_ENV=

# Sentry DSN for consent-gated JS crash reporting. LEAVE UNSET to disable
# entirely (fail-closed). Sentry only initialises when this is set AND the
# user has granted telemetry consent AND the session is not decoy/demo.
# See src/lib/sentry.js for the guards and scrubbing rules; when set, add
# an "Analytics/Diagnostics" purpose to Play Data Safety + Apple App Privacy
# and update /privacy to disclose crash reports.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# ── Staging ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Staging builds use .env.staging (checked in, no secrets).
# CI injects VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID from Actions variables.
# Supabase is intentionally blanked — staging must not write to prod.

# Vite base public path (only set if hosting under a sub-path).
VITE_BASE=

# --- RPC / indexer overrides (client-exposed, NOT secret) ---
# Override the default public endpoints for any chain family. All are UNTRUSTED
# infrastructure (reads + broadcast only; signing is always local on-device).
# Set in .env.local, never committed.
#
# Solana — replace the flaky public devnet RPC (e.g. Helius / QuickNode free tier):
VITE_SOL_RPC_URL_DEVNET=
VITE_SOL_RPC_URL_MAINNET=
# BTC Esplora:
VITE_BTC_ESPLORA_URL_TESTNET=
VITE_BTC_ESPLORA_URL_MAINNET=
# EVM (network key matches src/wallet-core/evm/networks.js, e.g. sepolia, mainnet):
VITE_EVM_RPC_URL_SEPOLIA=
VITE_EVM_RPC_URL_MAINNET=

# DEV-ONLY: flip the send gate so receive_only assets can be sent for testnet
# verification. Dead-code-eliminated from production builds. Set in .env.local,
# never inline (inline shell vars fail on Windows/PowerShell). See CLAUDE.md.
VITE_DEV_UNGATE_SEND=

# Phase 1b per-chain expansion — off by default; flip to 1 to preview
# USDC/USDT on Polygon/Arbitrum/Optimism/Avalanche/BNB (receive_only until
# on-chain send verified). See docs/per-chain-expansion-scope.md.
VITE_MULTI_CHAIN_ROWS=0

# --- Fiat on-ramp (Transak) — CLIENT-EXPOSED, NOT SECRET ---
# The Buy button is dead-code-eliminated from production builds unless
# VITE_BUY_ENABLED === 'true'. This is the SHIP GATE: flip it only when the
# Transak partner agreement is signed AND production API keys are issued.
# Staging builds may set it to 'true' with a STAGING partner key to exercise
# the flow end-to-end (see docs/transak-integration-spec.md).
VITE_BUY_ENABLED=false
# Transak partner API key. Public per-partner identifier (safe to ship in the
# bundle — sensitive operations are gated server-side by Transak). Baked in at
# build time; set BEFORE npm run android:run / mobile:build.
VITE_TRANSAK_API_KEY=
# STAGING (global-stg.transak.com) or PRODUCTION (global.transak.com). Must
# match the environment the API key was issued for.
VITE_TRANSAK_ENVIRONMENT=STAGING

# --- dApp Connector (WalletConnect v2 / Reown) — OPTIONAL; client-exposed, NOT secret ---
# A free project ID from dashboard.reown.com (formerly cloud.walletconnect.com).
# It is a PUBLIC client identifier (it ships in the bundle), NOT a key/secret.
# A committed public DEFAULT ships in src/wallet-core/evm/walletconnect/projectId.js,
# so the dApp Connector is enabled on EVERY build with no setup — this closes the
# recurring "Project ID required after an APK rebuild" bug (the ID used to live only
# in this git-ignored file, so worktree/clone/CI builds shipped it empty). Set this
# ONLY to override the default with your own Reown project. Any override is baked in
# at `vite build` time, so a MOBILE override must be set BEFORE `npm run mobile:build`
# / `npm run android:run` — there is no runtime .env on the device.
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# --- CryptoCompare (optional; client-exposed, NOT secret) ---
# Free API key from cryptocompare.com/cryptopian/api-keys. Without it the v2
# OHLCV endpoint (/data/v2/histo*) used by Price Charts may be rate-limited or
# CORS-blocked on Android, producing "Failed to load chart data: Failed to Fetch".
# Baked in at build time — set BEFORE npm run android:run / mobile:build.
VITE_CRYPTOCOMPARE_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter LLM — REMOVED (Codex P1 2026-08-15) ---
# The old VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY was VITE_-prefixed and so shipped in the
# client bundle — any user could extract it and spend Veyrnox's OpenRouter
# account. src/api/openrouterClient.js has been deleted. If AI features are
# re-introduced they MUST go through a server-side proxy (Supabase Edge
# Function pattern, matching tip-chat / tip-screen) so the key stays server-
# only. Do not re-add a VITE_ variable for an API secret.

# --- RevenueCat (in-app subscription: Safety Plus) — client-exposed, NOT secret ---
# Public per-platform SDK keys from app.revenuecat.com -> Project Settings -> API keys.
# These are safe to ship in the client bundle (RevenueCat treats them as public);
# the SECRET/server key must never appear here or anywhere in this repo. Native-only —
# web has no App Store/Play Store, so the web build ignores these entirely. Baked in at
# build time — set BEFORE npm run android:run / mobile:build.
VITE_REVENUECAT_APPLE_API_KEY=
VITE_REVENUECAT_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# Samsung Galaxy Store (RevenueCat purchases-store-galaxy module).
# Only needed for Samsung flavor builds (VITE_STORE_FLAVOR=samsung).
VITE_REVENUECAT_SAMSUNG_API_KEY=
# Optional Samsung billing mode override for Samsung flavor builds.
# Use TEST during Galaxy Store pre-release validation; production builds should
# resolve to PRODUCTION unless you deliberately need a test-mode build.
VITE_SAMSUNG_BILLING_MODE=
# Optional higher-tier offering id for AI Security Protection. Native-only; when blank,
# the AI plan card on /plans stays honest and says the offering is not configured in
# this build yet instead of surfacing a dead purchase path.
VITE_RC_AI_SECURITY_PROTECTION_OFFERING_ID=
# Optional AI referral discount path. Leave blank to keep AI referrals disabled
# even when the base AI offering exists.
VITE_RC_AI_REFERRAL_OFFERING_PREFIX=
# Optional AI cancel-save / retention offering id. Leave blank to keep AI
# retention offers disabled while Safety Plus continues using `retention`.
VITE_RC_AI_RETENTION_OFFERING_ID=
VITE_AI_SECURITY_PROTECTION_MONTHLY_PRICE_CENTS=
VITE_AI_SECURITY_PROTECTION_ANNUAL_PRICE_CENTS=
# Optional Supabase Edge Function overrides for the first-referral bonus grant.
# Leave blank to use the canonical entitlement ids already used in app code:
# `safety_plus` and `ai_security_protection`.
SAFETY_PLUS_REFERRAL_BONUS_ENTITLEMENT_ID=
AI_SECURITY_PROTECTION_REFERRAL_BONUS_ENTITLEMENT_ID=

# --- Referral tracker backend (OPTIONAL, Supabase; client-exposed, NOT secret) ---
# The lone backend touchpoint. Both are public client values — the anon key is
# designed to ship in the bundle; row-level security guards the table (see
# supabase/referrals.sql). Leave BOTH blank to disable referrals: registerCode/
# fetchStatus become no-ops and redeemCode returns 503 (src/api/referralApi.js).
# The table stores only { code, count } — no identity, addresses, or holdings.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- TIP remote threat screening (opt-in, off by default) ---
# Set this to the TIP deployment URL to SWITCH THE FEATURE ON. It is a feature
# flag only — the app does not call TIP directly with it; requests go through
# the tip-screen Supabase Edge Function, which needs VITE_SUPABASE_URL and
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY above. Leave blank and screening stays local-only.
VITE_TIP_BASE_URL=
#
# DO NOT ADD VITE_TIP_API_KEY OR VITE_TIP_SIGNING_SECRET (audit 2026-08-03 H-4).
# Every VITE_-prefixed variable is statically inlined into the shipped bundle,
# so a signing secret placed here would be handed to every user — and an HMAC
# scheme whose verifying secret the caller holds authenticates nothing.
# src/api/tipScreen.js REFUSES to build a client if either is set, disabling
# screening rather than running with a bundled secret.
#
# The real credentials belong in Supabase → Edge Functions → Secrets, as
# TIP_API_KEY and TIP_SIGNING_SECRET (no VITE_ prefix), alongside TIP_BASE_URL.
# See supabase/functions/tip-screen/index.ts.

# --- Testnet verification scripts ONLY (scripts/*.mjs) — SENSITIVE ---
# These are read by Node at runtime (process.env). Use a THROWAWAY testnet key
# that has only testnet funds. NEVER put a mainnet key or your real wallet seed
# here, and never commit a filled-in copy (.env.local is git-ignored).
SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=
# Provide EITHER a mnemonic OR a raw private key (testnet, disposable):
MNEMONIC=
PRIVATE_KEY=
# Optional send params for the proof scripts:
TO_ADDRESS=
AMOUNT_ETH=
